linux-thermal-control (0.5.13-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the real CPU package/Tctl sensor for Clevo fan control instead of
    presenting the hottest individual core as the package temperature.
  * Follow the lm-sensors fancontrol model with an eight-sample moving average
    and output hysteresis, while preserving an immediate raw-temperature
    100 percent safety response.
  * Show the filtered control temperature on the custom-curve graph while
    retaining the raw package reading in system telemetry.
  * Keep navigation selection derived solely from the active page so repeated
    clicks cannot toggle off the selected button color.

