linux-thermal-control (0.5.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Apply the current custom-curve target immediately when switching from
    full-speed instead of inheriting 100% and ramping down for nearly a minute.
  * Allow NVIDIA NVML to initialize on RTX Laptop drivers by disabling the
    incompatible ProtectClock systemd sandbox option while retaining the other
    daemon hardening settings.
  * Hide the blue live operating point when the active mode does not expose a
    known duty instead of displaying an artificial 100% value.
  * Add regression coverage for immediate full-speed to custom-curve switching.
  * Require acpi-call-dkms and gcc-12 so the verified Clevo backend is usable
    immediately after package installation on Ubuntu 22.04 HWE systems.
  * Keep unrelated controls visually stable during mode changes and cross-fade
    the confirmed mode selection instead of flashing the entire control page.
  * Stress-test every custom-curve interpolation segment through the runtime
    control loop, including observed mock RPM and the safety-temperature path.
  * Add D-Bus command/feedback closed-loop coverage and a guarded real-hardware
    test that validates ApplyZoneCurve replies, reported duty and four RPM feeds.

