linux-thermal-control (0.5.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Clevo acpi_call response parsing by truncating at the first NUL byte
    instead of deleting NUL bytes and concatenating stale kernel-buffer data.
  * Accept valid responses such as "0x69\\0alled" as 0x69 while preserving
    rejection of real ACPI error tokens.
  * Reload systemd and system D-Bus configuration before starting the daemon on
    first installation, and restart the service on fresh installs and upgrades.
  * Add ACPI response and maintainer-script regression tests.

